  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Drawings P029, P030, P031, P032, P033, P034, P035, P036 and P037 and Energy Statement(v2) and Transport Statement, received 08/06/2021. Drawings P130(A), P131(A), P133(B), P134(B), P137(B), P138(B), P139(B), P140(B) and P145(A), received 23/08/2021. Drawings P132(C), P135(C) and P136(C), received 07/09/2021) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development above ground level shall take place until full details and samples of all materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Details must include a detailed schedule of materials, a photographic sample board and rendered drawings, elevations and sections at a sufficient scale (1:20 or 1:50) to illustrate how all external materials will appear together.\r\nThe [samples/details] shall include: \r\n\"\tBrick/stonework (including brick, stone, masonry, brick panels, feature brick panel, brick framing feature and mortar on-site sample panel, minimum one metre by one metre) including all mortar colours, joint type, brick bond;\r\n\"\tCladding materials / render (including specifications where relevant);\r\n\"\tTiles / roof covering; including parapet coping / capping materials, dormers and canopies;\r\n\"\tWindow types; and sectional drawings of reveals / sills / head details \r\n\"\tBalcony details (including soffits, panels and frame);\r\n\"\tBalustrading treatment to balconies and roof areas (including details / sections / materials, and including handrail specifications)\r\n\"\tAny other materials/details / fittings to be used (including solar panels, extract vents, rainwater goods, boiler flues etc.), with sections and on-site samples where appropriate\r\nThe development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The development hereby permitted shall not be commenced until such time as final detailed designs of the boathouse have been submitted to, and approved in writing by, the local planning authority, in consultation with the Environment Agency. The designs will need to demonstrate the following:\r\n\"\tHow the flood defences are structurally independent of any non-flood defence structures;\r\n\"\tHow inspection and maintenance of the flood defences will be achieved.\r\nThe scheme shall be implemented in accordance with the agreed designs and maintained subsequently in perpetuity.",
    "Condition : 5 - The development shall not be occupied until space has been laid out within the site in accordance with approved plan no. P131(A) for 32 bicycles to be parked and that space shall thereafter be kept available for the parking of bicycles.",
    "Condition : 6 - The development shall not be occupied until the alterations to and improvements to the Thames Path and footway along Dan Mason Drive have been completed in accordance with the approved plans and made available to members of the public."
  ],
